  "name": "Gòge (Hausa fiddle dance music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Hausa dance and praise music led by the gòge one-string bowed fiddle with a calabash body and skin face, played for social dancing and entertainment as well as in bòòríí possession rites. Garba Liyo and Audu Yaron Goge were among its best-known recording artists, and Smithsonian Folkways issued Alhaji Garbo Leao and His Goge Music. The goje card stands in for the gòge and the inverted-calabash card for the calabash idiophones.",
